From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pp: post the sampled/draft feedback receive when it is consumed

VLLM_PP_DEFERRED_FEEDBACK_RECV=1 (default 0 = unchanged). Under PP the
non-last ranks receive step T's sampled tokens and drafts from the last rank
by an NCCL broadcast on a side stream, posted right after step T's forward
and consumed pp_size steps later. With several batches in flight the posted
receive spins an NCCL kernel on a few SMs for about pp_size stages, and every
Marlin MoE GEMM (persistent grid = all SMs) that overlaps it runs a second
wave: on MiMo PP4 at c32 the MoE GEMMs of ranks 0-2 took 401-504 us when
overlapped vs 243 us not (rank 3, which only sends, never overlaps). The
amount of overlap depends on the pipeline phase, which made steady-state
step time bistable (the same width ran at 12 or 16 ms per batch interval).

With the switch the receive stays queued with its metadata and its
broadcasts are issued (same collectives, same order) when the slot is
consumed at step T + pp_size, when the last rank has just sent it. Every
consumed slot is posted before any early return, so all ranks keep issuing
the group's collectives in the sender's order. Deferred receives are flushed
(FIFO) before the profiling run and graph capture (the last rank synchronizes
there with its warm-up sends outstanding), on empty steps, and in the worker
process before every RPC other than the per-step ones (execute_model,
sample_tokens, take_draft_token_ids, execute_dummy_batch): a profiler start or
any other RPC may synchronize the last rank while its sends are outstanding
and the other ranks wait in the same RPC (seen as an NCCL timeout on
start_profile under c32 load).
---
diff --git a/vllm/v1/executor/multiproc_executor.py b/vllm/v1/executor/multiproc_executor.py
index c86900d..3d7a381 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/executor/multiproc_executor.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/executor/multiproc_executor.py
@@ -595,6 +595,18 @@ class UnreadyWorkerProcHandle:
     death_writer: Connection | None = None
 
 
+_PP_STEP_RPCS = frozenset(
+    ("execute_model", "sample_tokens", "take_draft_token_ids", "execute_dummy_batch"))
+
+
+def _flush_pp_deferred(worker) -> None:
+    runner = getattr(worker, "model_runner", None)
+    handler = getattr(runner, "pp_handler", None)
+    flush = getattr(handler, "flush_deferred", None)
+    if flush is not None:
+        flush()
+
+
 @dataclass
 class WorkerProcHandle:
     proc: BaseProcess
@@ -1072,6 +1084,12 @@ class WorkerProc:
             elif isinstance(method, bytes):
                 func = partial(cloudpickle.loads(method), self.worker)
 
+            if method not in _PP_STEP_RPCS:
+                # VLLM_PP_DEFERRED_FEEDBACK_RECV: post this rank's deferred
+                # feedback receives before any non-step RPC (profiling, sleep,
+                # ...), which may synchronize the device on the last rank
+                # while its sends are outstanding.
+                _flush_pp_deferred(self.worker)
             output = func(*args, **kwargs)
 
             if output_rank is None or self.rank == output_rank:
